.TH OMF_RECORD_END 3 "OMF Format" "LIBOMF" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
omf_record_end - Get the end of an OMF record
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/omf/omf.h>
.PP
.B void* omf_record_end(omf_record* rec);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B omf_record_end
function returns a pointer to the end of an OMF record.
This pointer can be used to iterate over the data in the record.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I rec
A pointer to an
.B omf_record
structure representing the OMF record.
.SH RETURN VALUE
A pointer to the end of the OMF record.
.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the
.B omf_record_end
function:
.PP
.B #include <lib/omf/omf.h>
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.B int main() {
.B \tomf_file omf;
.B \tomf_record* rec = omf_read(&omf);
.B \tvoid* end = omf_record_end(rec);
.B \tprintf("End of record: %p\n", end);
.B \treturn 0;
.B }
.SH SEE ALSO
.B omf_init,
.B omf_read,
.B omf_record